+## Result
+
+2525 / KOU-21.16: **unsolved, 5/5**, with full independent scoped source/proof PASS.
+
+Five genuine turns give inverse-cost and exhaustion obstructions, finite-index and strong-kernel reductions, exact finite-action criteria, conjugacy exclusions, and compatible-product/Baire barriers. The original arbitrary-group separation remains unresolved.
+
+## Essential scope
+
+The positive set must algebraically generate every group element. Dense generation, a proper invariant semigroup, finite quotient diameters, or a bound for one symmetric generating set do not suffice. Compact/analytic restrictions and finite normal-generation assumptions remain explicit. Bergman and Rosendal are credited; no missing Khelif construction or historical novelty is asserted.
+
+The additive turn3 control-description clarification is retained prominently. All41 frozen author files and five review files are unchanged. Current README status supersedes only the historical pending-review wording, without editing it.
+
+## Verification
+
+All311,547 author controls,156 bindings and seven local source hashes replayed; the full independent audit adds6,833 controls and checks all five proofs. Portable replay uses Python's standard library. Optional source verification reports exactly the files supplied.
+
