+# Final result: Kourovka 21.16 remains unresolved after five turns
+
+**Proposed disposition: unsolved, 5/5; pending independent full source/proof review.** No separating group or universal equivalence proof has been obtained.
+
+## Exact target
+
+The October2026 Kourovka Notebook, Problem21.16, asks whether some group has finite diameter for every group-generating set, yet has an unbounded positive word metric for a set genuinely generating it as a monoid. Bounds may depend on the generating set. This is the separation part of Bergman's2006 Question9. Mere dense generation, a proper invariant semigroup, one bounded symmetric generating set, or strong/topological Bergman properties do not substitute for the target.
+
+## Five scoped outcomes
+
+1. **Inverse-cost obstruction:** in a CB group, positive diameter for S is finite exactly when inverses of S have uniformly bounded positive cost. A separating witness yields a proper subgroup exhaustion none of whose terms can be finitely supplemented to the whole group. Uniformly bounded-order witnesses are excluded.
+2. **Extension reductions:** MB passes to finite-index overgroups by positive Schreier rewriting. For a strongly bounded normal kernel, both CB and MB are equivalent upstairs and downstairs. The arbitrary MB-kernel extension question is not silently resolved.
+3. **Finite-action characterization:** a finite semidirect product is CB or MB precisely when its normal factor has the respective finite-width property for every invariant applicable generating set. Conjugate saturation can erase an unbounded positive witness, as the exact infinite-dihedral example demonstrates.
+4. **Conjugacy exclusions:** finitely normally generated CB groups have no conjugation-invariant or uniformly conjugacy-controlled unbounded positive witness. Uniform inverse-producing relations with a fixed finite supply of conjugators also force bounded positive diameter.
+5. **Limit/regularity barriers:** Cartesian positive sets with unbounded factor diameters fail algebraic generation of the full product; closed profinite sets satisfy an exact inverse-limit length formula. Genuine positive generation with Baire word balls on a compact group has finite diameter. The analytic compact-Polish consequence is credited prior theory, not an unrestricted abstract result.
+
+The remaining gap is to construct a genuinely monoid-generating S with unbounded inverse costs in an all-generating-set CB group of countable cofinality, or to prove this impossible. None of the restrictions above supplies that missing implication. The source permits arbitrary sets with no topology or definability assumptions.
+
+## Attribution and limits
+
+Bergman's countable-cofinality reduction is credited and reconstructed. Khelif's4-page announcement is reported only at its stated level; no missing HNN construction is invented or certified. Maltcev's chapter distinguishes the two generating conventions. Rosendal's stronger topological theorem and the classical analytic/Baire theorem are credited; their hypotheses are retained. No novelty certification is claimed for any structural lemma.
+
+TURN_3_CONTROL_CLARIFICATION.md corrects a test-description overstatement without altering frozen turn3 bytes or its proofs. The infinite dihedral diameter calculation is analytic; exact integer and finite local checks only support it.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+All checkers use Python3.10+ standard library:
+
+    python REPLAY_ALL.py
+
+The five byte-exact receipts contain311,547 assertions in total. These are exact finite controls supporting the written infinite-group arguments; they do not certify CB of an infinite group or prove the original. Optional `--sources PATH` verifies all seven primary PDFs. Raw PDFs, screenshots and imported source records are excluded from the public packet. Historical and final manifests bind the immutable author files.
+
+The fifth author turn is the stopping point. Only independent review and additive corrections or packaging should follow.
